A||||4||V8Fiero||Quantity of Coolant? SBC||||5||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||04-27-2001||09:10 PM||||Just wondering how many gallons of antifreeze you V8 guys/gals are running in your cooling system? (to acheive the 70/50 mix)<P>Thanks.<BR>Scott<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||hugh||04-27-2001||09:18 PM||||50/50 is the best ratio.Best way is to premix it and keep the 50/50 mix to add if necessary.||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||04-27-2001||09:22 PM||||I did the purging of the system per the Archie instruction tape. Got almost all the air out. Just wondering how much coolant to add to the system now.<P>A little tough to do the premix thing, wish I could though.......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks for your input hugh.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-27-2001||11:17 PM||||At this point, you need to get off your behind and get a coolant tester. That will tell you if the mix is weak real fast. Then you'll know if you need to add water or coolant to get it right. That is the only way you can do it without filling from dry with premix.<P>The coolant makers all spec 50/50 as the prefered mix. There is a premix chart in my cave. ( <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A> ) You are allowed up to 65-70% coolant depending on brand. Less than 50% and the additive package will be too weak to protect the system. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||04-27-2001||11:52 PM||||theogre:<P>Well according to the tester I used the first time said good to 245*. Ran my car for awhile and the coolant began to boil in the resevoir.(Not Good) Guage never went over 220. I tested it again and it showed good only to 225*. So obviously it wasnt mixed throughout the system very well. Im letting it cool down overnite and gonna add more coolant tomorrow. Will be approx 2.5 gallons in the system. Should be ok.<BR>Archie told me that he usually puts in 2 gallons.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by V8Fiero (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
